<section class="section" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">What ContentFlow App Is</p>
    <h2>A practical content operations interface, not a generic AI assistant.</h2>
    <p>
      The app connects planning, ideation, review, and scheduling around a
      consistent workspace model. It is designed for human decisions with
      continuity when backend services are degraded.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="split-grid">
    <article class="panel">
      <h3>Execution flow for operators</h3>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>authenticate into a workspace and resume activity immediately</li>
        <li>move through feed, editor, personas, ideas, and campaigns</li>
        <li>validate transitions with readable status and history</li>
        <li>leave clear evidence for review and handoff</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="panel">
      <h3>Continuity for unstable networks</h3>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>local cache supports read paths even when API sync is down</li>
        <li>outbound operations are queued as retryable actions</li>
        <li>reconciliation state is visible when connectivity returns</li>
        <li>diagnostics screens expose sync, uptime, and activity truthfully</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
